## What was checked
- Paired builds: 300 adaptive/writer-removed records compared with their original on the first two node arrays, first three element arrays and links; flagged 0. The adaptive arm adds one node and two elements (readout, writer); the writer-removed arm keeps the node and readout.
- Memory, development:adaptive: change -0.1934..+0.2269 V (mean |change| 0.0841); range over life 0.0142..0.2307 V; final-third slope max |1.48e-05| V/s; held exactly 0/30.
- Memory, development:writer_removed: change +0.0000..+0.0000 V (mean |change| 0.0000); range over life 0.0000..0.0000 V; final-third slope max |3.55e-19| V/s; held exactly 30/30.
- Memory, confirmation:adaptive: change -0.1185..+0.2368 V (mean |change| 0.0643); range over life 0.0061..0.2369 V; final-third slope max |5.01e-05| V/s; held exactly 0/120.
- Memory, confirmation:writer_removed: change +0.0000..+0.0000 V (mean |change| 0.0000); range over life 0.0000..0.0000 V; final-third slope max |2.80e-19| V/s; held exactly 120/120.
- The adaptive memory moves within each life (range above); the final-third slope is small but nonzero, and motion can ride the oscillation, so it is not evidence of a quiet settled knob.
- Saved traces of failed draws: 11/15 requested arm-traces available. Missing: [('confirmation', 2026120208, 'adaptive'), ('confirmation', 2026120208, 'writer_removed'), ('confirmation', 2026120221, 'adaptive'), ('confirmation', 2026120221, 'writer_removed')]. No replay was run to fill gaps.

